// Dual-wield scopes (game-thread processing and the weapon hooks) probe memory with guarded reads
// instead: VirtualQuery sizes the whole run of identical pages around the address, which inside the
// game's multi-hundred-megabyte heap regions costs milliseconds per call. The Stage 36 frame probe
// measured 400 ms per tick in the offhand arm check and 7 s in the left-holster marker lookup from
// these calls alone. The probe touches one byte per page (never a stack guard page: the dual paths
// only read game objects).
// v0.9.335: every readable check is a guarded probe now (MemoryProbe::Readable: a guard page tripped gets its guard
// back); the dual-wield scopes still make IsWritableRange a probe too (their writes are guarded themselves).
bool ProbeReadableRange(const void* address, std::size_t bytes) {
    return MemoryProbe::Readable(address, bytes);
}

bool ProbeCopyCString(const char* source, char* destination, std::size_t capacity) {
    return MemoryProbe::CopyCString(source, destination, capacity);
}

bool IsReadableRange(const void* address, std::size_t bytes) {
    return MemoryProbe::Readable(address, bytes);
}


























