// (FXEmitterInst::InitRender makes an FXEmitterDrawable for the scene; FXEmitterDrawable::Draw, TR2 0x400580, and the
// emitters' updates never look at the instance's DrawableComponent), and so are its FX lights' glows. The game turns
// them off by ending them. A hidden instance with an FX component (retail Instance::GetFXComponent 0x3DE6F0) has its FX
// ended (FX_EndFXInstanceEffects(instance, -1), retail 0x323FC0, TR2 0x346DF0: every general effect and emitter of it
// at once; the graceful one, retail 0x324130, lets the particles live their lives out, and a glow's may never end),
// again twice a second (a script may start them again). When it had some (FXComponent +0x324 bit 0,
